  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Underfunded Emergencies within the 2022 Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) for the Venezuela Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the context in each Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) country within the Latin America and Caribbean (LAC) region continues to evolve, migrants and refugees from Venezuela continue to need immediate and effective emergency assistance in the form of food assistance, health, humanitarian transportation, cash and voucher assistance, shelter, non-food items, water, sanitation and hygiene, among others. The proposed project, within the context of the RMRP, is primarily operating as a small grant mechanism, ensuring assistance is available to IOM missions in LAC to respond to emergencies regularly emerging in the field, involving migrants and refugees from Venezuela.</narrative>
  </description>
